msgstr ""

#: src/modules/dashboard/pages/Performance.jsx:43
msgid "Reduced Motion"
msgstr ""

#: src/modules/dashboard/pages/Performance.jsx:44
msgid "Visitors who have asked their operating system to reduce motion get no animation runtime at all — nothing plays, and nothing is downloaded."
msgstr ""

#: src/modules/dashboard/pages/Performance.jsx:63
msgid "GSAP and ScrollTrigger alone are about 114 KB. With this on they are not fetched until an animated element is close to the viewport, so a page whose animations are all below the fold starts with none of it. An element whose script has not arrived yet simply renders without animating — it is never left invisible."
msgstr ""

#: src/modules/dashboard/pages/Performance.jsx:67
msgid "Visitors who have asked their operating system to reduce motion get no animation runtime at all — nothing plays, and nothing is downloaded. Everyone else is unaffected."
msgstr ""

#: src/modules/dashboard/pages/Performance.jsx:71
msgid "Marks every image inside an animated element so cache plugins leave it alone. Those images then load normally instead of lazily, so keep the conditions narrow — the runtime already waits for a lazy image before animating it, and this is for the site that still has a problem."
msgstr ""

#: src/modules/dashboard/pages/Performance.jsx:75
msgid "On a page Elementor paints end to end, the theme's own CSS, fonts and jQuery render nothing — this stops them being loaded there. Only offered while the companion theme is active, and only where you allow it: exclude anything the theme still lays out itself, such as the blog, archives and search."
msgstr ""

